 @BlindTrustProject that’s extremely difficult to say given that they’re built on different architectures, different die size and processing chips (4 nm vs 5 nm), different number of units, different vram etc. For example the 5070 ti has a larger die size, faster/better vram, more shading units. 
Therefore, it’s very difficult to compare between architecture cus the 9070 xt will be stronger in some areas and the 5070 ti stronger.

Also, the improvement in performance isn’t significant enough to call launch drivers sub-par but current drivers “where they should be” cus even in the video Steve says it doesn’t change much performance wise between these two cards.

